{"headword":"יִשַׁי","parent_lexicon":"BDB Dictionary","content":{"senses":[{"definition":"<strong>n.pr.m.</strong> father of David <strong>(</strong>etym. dub.; Ol<sup>§ 277 f.</sup> conj. <span dir=\"rtl\">יֵשׁ יָהּ</span>; We <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 14:49\" href=\"/I_Samuel.14.49\">1 S 14:49</a> <span dir=\"rtl\">ישׁי</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">אישׁי</span> = <span dir=\"rtl\">אבישׁי</span> (but see this)<strong>)</strong>—<span dir=\"rtl\">יִשַׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16:3\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16.3\">1 S 16:3</a> + 29 times; <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשָׁ֑י</span> v <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16:19\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16.19\">19</a> + 10 times; 𝔊 Ιεσσαι; <span dir=\"rtl\">(וְ)אִישַׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:13\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.13\">1 Ch 2:13</a>;—+ <span dir=\"rtl\">יִשַׁי בֵּית־הַלַּחְמִי</span> <em>Jesse the Bethlehemite</em> <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16:1\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16.1\">1 S 16:1</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16:18\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16.18\">18</a> (<span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־ישׁי וגו׳</span>, of David), <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17:58\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17.58\">17:58</a>†; <span dir=\"rtl\">ישׁי</span> also <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16:3\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16.3\">16:3</a> + 14 times <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 16\" href=\"/I_Samuel.16\">1 S 16</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17\">17</a>; †son of <span dir=\"rtl\">עוֹבֵד</span> according to <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:17\" href=\"/Ruth.4.17\">Ru 4:17</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ruth 4:22\" href=\"/Ruth.4.22\">22</a><sup>(×2)</sup> = <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 2:12\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.2.12\">1 Ch 2:12</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">דָּוִ(י)ד בֶּן־ישׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 23:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.23.1\">2 S 23:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 10:14\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.10.14\">1 Ch 10:14</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 29:26\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.29.26\">29:26</a> <a data-ref=\"Psalms 72:20\" href=\"/Psalms.72.20\">ψ 72:20</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">אֱלִיאָב בֶּן־ישׁי</span> <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 11:18\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.11.18\">2 Ch 11:18</a>; elsewhere <span dir=\"rtl\">בֶּן־ישׁי</span> alone = David, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:27\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.27\">1 S 20:27</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:30\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.30\">30</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 20:31\" href=\"/I_Samuel.20.31\">31</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:7\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.7\">22:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:8\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.8\">8</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:9\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.9\">9</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:13\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.13\">13</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 25:10\" href=\"/I_Samuel.25.10\">25:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 20:1\" href=\"/II_Samuel.20.1\">2 S 20:1</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Kings 12:16\" href=\"/I_Kings.12.16\">1 K 12:16</a> = <a data-ref=\"II Chronicles 10:16\" href=\"/II_Chronicles.10.16\">2 Ch 10:16</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 12:18\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.12.18\">1 Ch 12:18</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">גֶּזַע יִשָׁ֑י</span> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 11:1\" href=\"/Isaiah.11.1\">Is 11:1</a>; <span dir=\"rtl\">שֹׁרֶשׁ יִשַׁי</span> v <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 11:10\" href=\"/Isaiah.11.10\">10</a> of Jesse as ancestor of future (Messianic) king†."}]},"rid":"BDB04249","strong_numbers":["3448"],"next_hw":"יָשִׁיב","prev_hw":"יָשַׁט","occurrences":"41","quotes":[],"GK":["3805","414"],"TWOT":["926"],"parent_lexicon_details":{"name":"BDB Dictionary","language":"heb.biblical","to_language":"eng","text_categories":[],"source":"BDB Dictionary","attribution":"F. Brown, S. Driver & C. Briggs","index_title":"BDB","version_title":"A Hebrew and English lexicon of the Old Testament, by Francis Brown. With the co-operation of S. R. Driver and Charles A. Briggs. Oxford, 1906","version_lang":"en","should_autocomplete":true}}